From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:16:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 083/202] [ae-patch] Show one right-hand pane at a time when
 the session rail and a panel do not both fit

With the session rail and the workspace panel both open in a window too
narrow for both, the rail floated over the workspace panel and hid its
right half.

When the open rail would float over an open workspace, files or logs
panel, the pane opened last now stays and the other closes. Opening the
rail closes the push panels and, through the shell's own toggle, the
workspace panel. Opening a panel, narrowing the window, widening the
sidebar or switching to a session whose workspace panel is open closes
the rail instead and marks it closedForPanel, saved with the rail's
layout; the rail reopens as it was once no panel needs the room, and a
rail the user opens or closes clears the mark. The check runs in a
layout effect, so the overlap never paints.
